              "answers": [
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "The nausea and vomiting caused by opioids can be decreased by ‘…setron’ drugs like ondansetron or sometimes by lying down\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "The respiratory depression caused by opioid consumption is caused by a decreased sensitivity of the brainstem to rising levels of carbon dioxide \n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect, the itch after opioid consumption is caused by a release of histamine&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>That is right, the itch after opioid consumption is caused by a release of histamine</div>\n",
                    "tip": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>The itch caused by opioid consumption is due to components of the drug binding to epithelial cells</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>The combination of pinpoint pupils and respiratory depression is invaluable in indicating the use of Naloxone, the opioid antagonist (the antidote for opioid overdose)</div>\n"
                  },
                  "text": "<div>The pinpoint pupils of a person with opioid overdose can be a valuable sign that points to opioid overdose rather than other drugs.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Indeed, this is due to the fact that opioids decrease the body's natural opioids and decreases the receptors for opioids.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "tip": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>Actually this is true, and this is due to the fact that opioids decrease the body's natural opioids and decreases the receptors for opioids.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Clients who have been taking opioids for over three weeks often come back complaining of increased pain.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                }
